module

public import Transformer.Grokking.FlatSpectrum.TablePart.Rectangles

/-!
# PT6: the training cells of the tables without the column `b = 0`

Source: `review/flat_spectrum.md`, *What a part of the table determines*, PT6. At `p = 17`, `97` and
`193` five tasks share a table without the column `b = 0` and one split. The masks below are their
training cells, and the lists are two rectangles of these cells for each task outside the class.
These are data of the experiment, and the kernel does not rerun its shuffle on them. The tests
`lean_div_masks_are_the_training_cells` and `lean_div_witnesses_are_training_cells` of
`experiments/table_part` read this file and check it against the real split.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Transformer.Grokking.FlatSpectrum.TablePart.E6

